<title>CANADA: Goodale to keep Canada Wheat Board portfolio.</title>
<headline>Goodale to keep Canada Wheat Board portfolio.</headline>
<dateline>OTTAWA 1997-06-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ralph Goodale will retain responsibility for the Canadian Wheat Board export monopoly after being replaced in his current post as agriculture minister, Prime Minister Jean Chretien's spokesman Peter Donolo said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Media reports had said that Goodale would become natural resources minister, but would keep the Wheat Board responsibility.</p>
<p>Donolo said the Wheat Board responsibility was natural for a minister from the wheat-growing province of Saskatchewan.</p>
<p>Goodale oversaw a farmers' referendum that rejected abandoning the Wheat Board monopoly on the export of barley.</p>
<p>((Ottawa Reuters Bureau 613-235-6745))</p>
